                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 200,
                            "last_played": 1792826475
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Solid little breakout game, it's not as precise as you'd expect, once you get the angles down it's pretty easy to cruise through it.\r\n\r\nThe slow down, speed up, and weapon mechanics are fun. The story, is a bit eh, but it's nice that there's something at all. The exploration segments in story mode are a bit... unresponsive, but they aren't difficult. It's fun that they have different little puzzles for each area.\r\n\r\nThe biggest bummer is that the dev hasn't finished the endings he has 9, but listed 18, and one of his posts just says that he ran out of time and resources to work on them. Maybe in the future somethime.\r\n\r\nEither way though, good game, fun, and maybe a couple hours to get the main content done with, there's  a lot of little side content to grind out, and a level maker? which is pretty neat.",
